adverb can <span class=\"italic\">sometimes</span>  be in different positions in the sentence. For example, you put the adverb of frequency after the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be</span> . "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">always</span> go to yoga class on Wednesdays."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Susan <span class=\"strong\"> rarely</span> eats breakfast. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Robert <span class=\"strong\">never</span> drinks tea."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "always"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at all times"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I always have coffee in the morning."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about daily activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "never"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not ever; at no time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I never take the bus to school."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "usually"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "regularly; normally"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I usually have a sandwich for lunch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sometimes"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "now and then; not all the time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I sometimes go to the market when I need bread."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take a bre